WEBVTT

00:00:12.630 --> 00:00:18.210
The Magnificent
KOTOBUKI

00:00:19.540 --> 00:00:22.710
Flying through the mesh of clouds

00:00:22.710 --> 00:00:26.290
Our dancing wings wrap up in the wind

00:00:26.290 --> 00:00:29.710
Stars fall right before our eyes

00:00:35.750 --> 00:00:39.010
The blue of all blues that drew us in

00:00:39.010 --> 00:00:42.310
We kicked up off the blurring ground

00:00:42.310 --> 00:00:47.290
Let me hear the sound of the sky you know

00:00:49.880 --> 00:00:56.610
Take flight make gravity your ally

00:00:56.610 --> 00:01:03.040
One more time, however many 
times, laughing all along

00:01:03.040 --> 00:01:10.080
We would never look back when we fly

00:01:10.080 --> 00:01:15.360
An everlasting dream we 
live in pursuit of tomorrow

00:01:15.360 --> 00:01:18.790
Amid rising despair I locked away my love

00:01:18.790 --> 00:01:21.080
I hate my weak self

00:01:21.790 --> 00:01:27.040
Here and now passes by as 
we head towards the future

00:01:32.960 --> 00:01:37.830
Oh, great. Here I was ready for my chance to meet her,
but all I get is you, Saneatsu.

00:01:37.830 --> 00:01:40.080
The Madame stayed behind in Rahama.

00:01:40.500 --> 00:01:42.960
The place is just buzzing 
with air pirates right now.

00:01:42.960 --> 00:01:45.040
You want me to believe they 
just fly right into town?

00:01:45.040 --> 00:01:47.500
They really do lately, that's the thing!

00:01:47.500 --> 00:01:52.710
The Splendid Areshima

00:01:48.250 --> 00:01:51.130
I wish we could just do runs between
Rahama and Areshima forever!

00:01:51.130 --> 00:01:52.710
Or even just move to Areshima for good!

00:01:52.710 --> 00:01:55.080
It's quite an orderly, well regulated place.

00:01:55.420 --> 00:01:57.000
It's beauty is in its righteousness.

00:01:57.000 --> 00:01:58.080
Is it, now?

00:01:58.080 --> 00:01:58.880
Tell me though, Chika.

00:01:59.330 --> 00:02:02.080
Surely you don't plan on keeping
that in our quarters, yes?

00:02:02.080 --> 00:02:03.130
Absolutely not.

00:02:03.130 --> 00:02:04.380
If just because it is unreasonably bulky.

00:02:04.380 --> 00:02:07.170
What? But it's so fluffy! Look at this fluff!

00:02:07.170 --> 00:02:08.100
It's an anomalocaris.

00:02:08.790 --> 00:02:11.270
In ancient times, it thrived 
in the oceans, vast

00:02:11.270 --> 00:02:14.280
expanses of water rich in 
salt and other minerals.

00:02:14.280 --> 00:02:16.500
Cool! Oceans, huh?

00:02:16.830 --> 00:02:18.150
How could you not know that?

00:02:18.150 --> 00:02:20.920
Well, oceans haven't existed 
for a long time now, after all.

00:02:20.920 --> 00:02:22.550
Chika's subconscious might have driven her

00:02:22.550 --> 00:02:24.990
to seek something ocean related 
without her realizing it.

00:02:25.000 --> 00:02:27.170
Bingo! Kate, you sure know your stuff!

00:02:27.170 --> 00:02:29.210
And just how much did that cost you?

00:02:29.210 --> 00:02:31.670
498 pounds and 98 sen!

00:02:31.670 --> 00:02:32.170
Wha...?!

00:02:32.170 --> 00:02:33.420
Oh let her be.

00:02:33.420 --> 00:02:35.750
We all use our earnings in different ways.

00:02:35.750 --> 00:02:39.630
Be it to buy stuffed animals, to drown
in some good drink, or simply stuff our faces.

00:02:39.630 --> 00:02:41.290
And speaking of that, where's Kylie?

00:02:43.380 --> 00:02:44.250
Delish!

00:02:44.250 --> 00:02:47.000
A flavor unlike the pancakes of
either Rahama or the Hagoromo!

00:02:47.000 --> 00:02:48.210
Heya dimwit!

00:02:48.630 --> 00:02:50.610
I'm certain I told you all of us needed to

00:02:50.610 --> 00:02:54.380
submit flying
applications to the Areshima airway authorities.

00:02:54.380 --> 00:02:56.540
We never used to have to.

00:02:56.540 --> 00:02:57.440
That's so totalitarian.

00:02:57.440 --> 00:02:59.180
Like it or not, the law is the law and you

00:02:59.180 --> 00:03:01.980
cannot just go ignoring it 
and doing whatever you want.

00:03:01.980 --> 00:03:04.580
I had a feeling it wouldn't fly.

00:03:04.580 --> 00:03:07.170
But once I saw the word 
"pancakes" I just lost control!

00:03:07.170 --> 00:03:08.910
I'm sure you know how it can be, right?

00:03:08.910 --> 00:03:09.620
I do not.

00:03:09.620 --> 00:03:12.540
You ever get so caught up in something that
you lose sight of everything else?

00:03:12.540 --> 00:03:13.210
I do not.

00:03:13.210 --> 00:03:14.710
Or just set off headstrong 
down the wrong path?

00:03:14.710 --> 00:03:15.460
No!

00:03:16.830 --> 00:03:18.050
No...

00:03:18.050 --> 00:03:21.340
Reona would never ever get caught 
up in something and rush on

00:03:21.340 --> 00:03:23.050
ahead without thinking, now would you?

00:03:23.050 --> 00:03:23.590
Would you?!

00:03:23.590 --> 00:03:24.300
No!

00:03:24.830 --> 00:03:27.380
At any rate, you need to let someone know
before you go running off like that.

00:03:27.380 --> 00:03:28.310
Yeah, yeah!

00:03:28.310 --> 00:03:29.290
What a lame excuse for a fighter pilot!

00:03:29.290 --> 00:03:31.380
What's the deal with that hideous doll?

00:03:31.380 --> 00:03:32.540
It's an anomalocaris!

00:03:32.540 --> 00:03:34.290
The subconscious of all ocean life!

00:03:34.290 --> 00:03:35.420
Sounds like gibberish.

00:03:35.420 --> 00:03:37.250
Woosh! Smash!

00:03:37.250 --> 00:03:37.830
One down!

00:03:37.830 --> 00:03:39.210
What's your deal, you doofus?!

00:03:39.210 --> 00:03:39.830
Hey! Stop it!

00:03:39.630 --> 00:03:40.580
Get back here!

00:03:40.580 --> 00:03:41.460
Stop!

00:03:42.540 --> 00:03:44.040
Oh my, a passenger vehicle?

00:03:44.040 --> 00:03:45.420
A modified Tudor Model AA.

00:03:45.420 --> 00:03:49.620
To think we'd see a non-cargo automobile.
Areshima sure is full of surprises.

00:03:48.080 --> 00:03:50.040
Oh my goodness!

00:03:50.040 --> 00:03:51.500
Are you all right? Are you hurt?

00:03:51.500 --> 00:03:52.710
How are you feeling?

00:03:52.710 --> 00:03:53.500
Uhh...

00:03:53.500 --> 00:03:54.960
Oh thank goodness you're okay.

00:03:54.960 --> 00:03:56.460
I'm so relieved, and super sorry!

00:03:56.460 --> 00:03:57.630
Think of this as an apology.

00:03:57.630 --> 00:03:58.380
That's chump change!

00:03:58.380 --> 00:03:59.460
But I'll take it!

00:03:59.460 --> 00:04:01.170
Woah! How did you do that?!

00:04:01.170 --> 00:04:01.880
A little giftey for you!

00:04:01.880 --> 00:04:03.420
Sir, we must be going.

00:04:03.420 --> 00:04:05.050
Yeah, yeah, just a minute.

00:04:05.050 --> 00:04:09.040
From now on, make sure you look
right, left, down, and right again! Got it?

00:04:09.040 --> 00:04:09.880
Okay!

00:04:09.880 --> 00:04:11.100
Thank you! Wonderful! You have my gratitude!

00:04:11.100 --> 00:04:13.040
And that anomalocaris! I'm a fan.

00:04:16.750 --> 00:04:17.710
Don't run off like that!

00:04:17.710 --> 00:04:18.830
Don't shout like that!

00:04:18.830 --> 00:04:19.880
Quit causing such a ruckus!

00:04:19.880 --> 00:04:21.450
Quit causing trouble for the rest of us!

00:04:21.450 --> 00:04:23.580
Can't you just be quiet for a change-

00:04:26.080 --> 00:04:27.920
Somebody! Do something about this bird!

00:04:27.920 --> 00:04:30.380
That "bird" is Captain Dodo.

00:04:30.380 --> 00:04:31.700
I don't care!

00:04:31.700 --> 00:04:34.460
It's a message from First Officer Saneatsu.

00:04:34.460 --> 00:04:37.040
"Head for the Ocean Sunfish Hotel ASAP."

00:04:37.460 --> 00:04:42.010
My goodness, just where were you
Kotoboofy Fright Snore girls off wandering?

00:04:42.380 --> 00:04:45.000
What can we do for you, Councilor Julia?

00:04:45.000 --> 00:04:46.290
Take a seat.

00:04:46.290 --> 00:04:48.470
You're making it look like 
I'm just picking on you.

00:04:48.960 --> 00:04:51.500
Two days from now I have
a god-awful sort of meeting here.

00:04:51.500 --> 00:04:54.170
You can get the details 
from my chief of security.

00:04:54.170 --> 00:04:55.710
You'll be handling the air situation.

00:04:55.710 --> 00:04:58.030
What sort of "meeting" might this be?

00:04:58.030 --> 00:04:59.250
And who is it with?

00:04:59.250 --> 00:05:01.210
I cannot simply promise our services
without knowing the details as to-

00:05:01.210 --> 00:05:04.290
I will be meeting with the 
head of View Trading, Isao.

00:05:04.290 --> 00:05:06.630
A man dubbed likely to be 
the next head of Ikesuka.

00:05:06.630 --> 00:05:07.130
What?

00:05:07.130 --> 00:05:07.830
"Isao?"

00:05:07.830 --> 00:05:08.670
Never heard of him!

00:05:09.540 --> 00:05:12.620
He has plans to deal with the air pirate
and energy problems.

00:05:12.620 --> 00:05:16.200
Insisting on using the capital and connections of
major corporations,

00:05:16.200 --> 00:05:18.580
making himself a hero to the public.

00:05:18.580 --> 00:05:20.420
But I can't stand him.

00:05:20.420 --> 00:05:23.670
He's trying to influence politics with
his idealist words and assumption of intrinsic good.

00:05:23.670 --> 00:05:26.540
Traveling the world thanks to a seemingly lucky streak
and a massive fortune alone.

00:05:26.540 --> 00:05:28.800
The most devious man you'll ever meet.

00:05:28.800 --> 00:05:31.960
And I absolutely despise those 
awful magic tricks of his.

00:05:31.960 --> 00:05:36.470
I've about had it with this useless excuse of
a man poking his nose into political affairs.

00:05:36.470 --> 00:05:38.420
And this "meeting" is the worst of it!

00:05:38.420 --> 00:05:40.660
I wish I could tell him to shove it and be done,


00:05:40.660 --> 00:05:43.230
but I'd never hear the end, 
so I'm going through with it.

00:05:43.230 --> 00:05:49.250
All he proposes about national unification,
mutual benefits, justice, safety, duty, and power--

00:05:49.250 --> 00:05:50.380
It's all garbage!

00:05:50.380 --> 00:05:52.710
And if he really does believe in all that,
then he's got crap for brains!

00:05:52.710 --> 00:05:54.480
And now we live in the darkest 
of timelines where even

00:05:54.480 --> 00:05:56.900
people on the council have 
begun yielding to him.

00:05:56.900 --> 00:06:00.750
If I'm gonna sit through this meeting,
he's going to get a nice solid choking out of it!

00:06:00.750 --> 00:06:02.040
Sounds rough...

00:06:02.040 --> 00:06:06.580
Anyway that's why I need to prepare
in case these air pirates-

00:06:06.580 --> 00:06:09.290
-if they are even air pirates at all...

00:06:09.290 --> 00:06:11.540
Aren't apt to like this arrangement one bit.

00:06:11.540 --> 00:06:15.960
I don't plan to get all friendly with Isao,
but I certainly don't need air pirates interfering.

00:06:15.960 --> 00:06:19.230
Especially when they seem to get
their hands on whatever intel they want.

00:06:19.230 --> 00:06:22.330
And if that means I need to protect
that good-for-nothing Isao, so be it.

00:06:22.330 --> 00:06:24.670
Surely you could ask Areshima 
security for assistance?

00:06:24.670 --> 00:06:27.580
Of course I can, but I'd rather not be left
with a debt to any city in Ikesuka.

00:06:27.580 --> 00:06:29.500
And so you want our help instead.

00:06:29.500 --> 00:06:30.830
Are we finally on the same page?

00:06:30.830 --> 00:06:34.460
Without the Madame present,
this decision rests with our First Officer.

00:06:34.460 --> 00:06:36.330
Not like he's the brightest bulb...

00:06:36.330 --> 00:06:37.960
I too am a bulb!

00:06:37.960 --> 00:06:41.710
One that shines day and night,
only to light the way before you!

00:06:41.710 --> 00:06:43.380
Hey! You're the flower guy!

00:06:43.920 --> 00:06:44.960
What's this? Do I have a fan?

00:06:44.960 --> 00:06:46.590
Really? Why? What do you like best?

00:06:46.590 --> 00:06:48.630
My face? My voice? My charm? All of it?

00:06:48.630 --> 00:06:50.320
How embarrassing! How wonderful!

00:06:50.320 --> 00:06:52.430
I'm so happy I feel I could just burst!

00:06:52.430 --> 00:06:53.960
Look at all that glitter!

00:06:53.960 --> 00:06:55.890
You never cease to disgust me.

00:06:56.380 --> 00:06:59.350
Do you ever run out of your 
street corner tricks, Mr. Isao?

00:06:59.350 --> 00:07:01.580
Lady Councilor, your meeting is with him...?

00:07:01.580 --> 00:07:03.040
I'm quite shocked.

00:07:03.040 --> 00:07:04.710
Oh, you're familiar?

00:07:04.710 --> 00:07:06.210
That makes things easier, then.

00:07:06.210 --> 00:07:08.460
Let me introduce you, Isao.

00:07:08.460 --> 00:07:12.170
These are the girls of the KOTOBUKI Flight Corps
who will be handling security.

00:07:12.170 --> 00:07:13.170
And their leader, Reona.

00:07:13.170 --> 00:07:15.630
Well, well! Well met there, Miss Leader!

00:07:16.040 --> 00:07:17.000
Here's a little giftey for ya!

00:07:17.330 --> 00:07:19.460
What? Oh... Thank you.

00:07:20.290 --> 00:07:21.750
Gotcha! Gotcha good!

00:07:21.750 --> 00:07:23.170
Woops, sorry, did that hurt?

00:07:23.170 --> 00:07:26.000
It shouldn't be that bad, what's wrong?

00:07:26.000 --> 00:07:27.000
Yeowch!

00:07:27.000 --> 00:07:28.380
Just kidding!

00:07:28.960 --> 00:07:30.040
What's the plan?

00:07:30.040 --> 00:07:32.840
The problem will be with how we coordinate
with the security units.

00:07:32.840 --> 00:07:33.500
What?!

00:07:33.500 --> 00:07:34.960
Reona, are you seriously 
thinking of doing this?

00:07:34.960 --> 00:07:35.670
No thanks!

00:07:35.670 --> 00:07:37.540
I'm in! I wanna see some action this time!

00:07:37.540 --> 00:07:39.850
We don't even know how many people 
we'll be up against or where they're

00:07:39.850 --> 00:07:41.350
coming from. Isn't this a tad rash?

00:07:41.350 --> 00:07:44.170
I already have plans that day.

00:07:44.170 --> 00:07:45.750
Plans I cannot change.

00:07:46.210 --> 00:07:48.210
So that's one "yes" and two "no".

00:07:48.210 --> 00:07:51.360
And counting me that's two 
of us with some reservations.

00:07:51.360 --> 00:07:53.580
No, we should take this.

00:07:53.580 --> 00:07:54.420
We need it.

00:07:54.420 --> 00:07:55.330
Why?

00:07:55.670 --> 00:07:58.960
Defending Rahama cost us lots
in repairs and maintenance.

00:07:58.960 --> 00:08:00.710
We need to make up for that.

00:08:00.710 --> 00:08:01.370
Well...

00:08:01.370 --> 00:08:02.380
Why?!

00:08:02.380 --> 00:08:04.330
You never gave Chika trouble 
when she went down!

00:08:04.330 --> 00:08:06.000
I thought we were supposed 
to be treated equal here!

00:08:06.000 --> 00:08:06.960
I'm not blaming you.

00:08:07.460 --> 00:08:09.040
I'm simply saying we should do this.

00:08:09.670 --> 00:08:10.630
This is tyranny!

00:08:10.630 --> 00:08:13.040
We're supposed to talk these things out!

00:08:13.040 --> 00:08:14.040
Stupid Reona!

00:08:13.500 --> 00:08:15.170
Leave my lil' Malo alone!

00:08:16.180 --> 00:08:17.580
Stop it!

00:08:17.580 --> 00:08:18.470
Change of schedule.

00:08:18.470 --> 00:08:20.830
Tomorrow I will wake up at 0700.

00:08:20.830 --> 00:08:23.420
I will spend fifteen minutes
on breakfast instead of thirty five.

00:08:23.750 --> 00:08:26.960
And I will no longer spend an hour and
forty five minutes staring off into space.

00:08:27.830 --> 00:08:29.420
What's the deal, Reona?

00:08:29.420 --> 00:08:30.960
This isn't like you.

00:08:30.960 --> 00:08:32.040
I almost forgot.

00:08:33.040 --> 00:08:34.790
Here's the ten sen I borrowed today.

00:08:35.210 --> 00:08:36.830
I don't like to stay in debt.

00:08:36.830 --> 00:08:39.910
That's our tenacious Reona.

00:08:40.210 --> 00:08:41.330
Maybe she's in love?

00:08:41.330 --> 00:08:42.020
Love?!

00:08:42.020 --> 00:08:45.080
She started acting strange as soon
as he came into the picture, right?

00:08:45.080 --> 00:08:47.040
Woah... "Love"...

00:08:47.040 --> 00:08:49.000
She should've just said something.

00:08:49.000 --> 00:08:54.130
I cannot say it is a feeling I am familiar with,
but it is a necessity of species survival.

00:08:54.500 --> 00:08:57.250
If it's true, I'd love to support her.

00:08:57.750 --> 00:09:02.080
But it's tough to imagine someone like
Reona succumbing to such.

00:09:02.080 --> 00:09:03.460
Why don't you simply ask?

00:09:03.460 --> 00:09:07.080
You don't know or do you?
Or do you know, but don't want us to know? Which is it?

00:09:07.080 --> 00:09:08.170
I'll go with answer one.

00:09:08.170 --> 00:09:09.330
That means she doesn't know.

00:09:09.330 --> 00:09:10.080
What?!

00:09:10.790 --> 00:09:13.210
Oh, but I can tell you 
something she sure hates.

00:09:13.210 --> 00:09:14.130
What's that?

00:09:14.130 --> 00:09:15.170
She hates being in debt.

00:09:15.170 --> 00:09:16.580
I'm fairly certain everyone does.

00:09:16.580 --> 00:09:19.420
Yeah, except maybe brainless 
dolts like Chika!

00:09:19.420 --> 00:09:20.750
Who you calling a dolt?

00:09:20.750 --> 00:09:22.710
Debts are meant to be shirked!

00:09:22.710 --> 00:09:24.130
An astonishing view on finance.

00:09:37.960 --> 00:09:38.720
What's this?

00:09:38.720 --> 00:09:41.880
What's our thunderbolt Kylie doing
with that sort of look on her face?

00:09:41.880 --> 00:09:43.130
Are you okay?

00:09:43.130 --> 00:09:44.580
Aren't you on the clock?

00:09:44.580 --> 00:09:46.670
Can love drive one to despotism?

00:09:46.670 --> 00:09:47.420
What?!

00:09:47.420 --> 00:09:49.000
That's the girl from the Hagoromo...

00:09:49.000 --> 00:09:50.630
Jeez, just what we don't need.

00:09:50.630 --> 00:09:52.000
And she's not alone.

00:09:52.000 --> 00:09:54.580
That's one, two, three...yikes! 
You're kidding!

00:09:54.580 --> 00:09:58.370
With everyone quitting or getting 
shot down, we're the only

00:09:58.370 --> 00:10:00.900
two left in the Nazarin, but look at them...

00:10:01.250 --> 00:10:04.750
I'm not even sure we can
call ourselves a "squad" anymore.

00:10:04.750 --> 00:10:05.700
Oh, hey...

00:10:06.460 --> 00:10:08.330
Who are you again? What was it...

00:10:08.330 --> 00:10:09.750
The Nazarin Air Squad!

00:10:09.750 --> 00:10:11.210
Oh yeah! That's it!

00:10:11.210 --> 00:10:12.670
You're looking good! That's great!

00:10:12.670 --> 00:10:14.720
We're just here filling in...

00:10:14.720 --> 00:10:16.080
Hey, so tell me.

00:10:16.710 --> 00:10:19.010
Can love drive someone to despotism?

00:10:19.970 --> 00:10:21.970
The Magnificent
KOTOBUKI

00:10:22.420 --> 00:10:23.880
I see, I see.

00:10:23.880 --> 00:10:27.250
So you want to put the priority on free will,
is it, Lady Julia?

00:10:27.250 --> 00:10:29.280
I take it you've got your 
own thoughts on the subject?

00:10:29.280 --> 00:10:32.710
Well, is one really free with freedom?

00:10:32.710 --> 00:10:35.960
It's hard to do anything when 
you're free to do everything.

00:10:35.960 --> 00:10:37.880
Plus we still have limits 
and responsibilities.

00:10:37.880 --> 00:10:41.700
You'd be surprised how many people can't keep up with
those.

00:10:41.700 --> 00:10:45.580
In the end, people just go on about all
they want to do, and it gets out of hand.

00:10:45.580 --> 00:10:46.670
To put it simply!

00:10:46.670 --> 00:10:50.750
It's like going out for a barbecue, trying to grill everything
at once, and just ending up with burnt food!

00:10:50.750 --> 00:10:54.250
And if we were to decide the order the food
was to be cooked, who would make those rules?

00:10:54.250 --> 00:10:57.050
You'll find there are many who would like to use
the rules and power to their own advantage.

00:10:57.050 --> 00:10:58.130
You tell 'em!

00:10:58.130 --> 00:10:58.920
Down with all rules!

00:10:58.920 --> 00:11:01.420
Kylie, you and the councilor 
might actually get along.

00:11:00.750 --> 00:11:03.010
Lady Julia, you need to have more faith!

00:11:01.420 --> 00:11:02.500
Ew, no way!

00:11:03.250 --> 00:11:07.130
I think, I believe, and I'm sure 
the world is a better place!

00:11:07.130 --> 00:11:07.960
And?

00:11:07.960 --> 00:11:08.750
Huh?

00:11:09.250 --> 00:11:10.770
My my! What might this be?

00:11:11.250 --> 00:11:13.630
Perhaps someone here has made
some unfortunate enemies?

00:11:13.630 --> 00:11:16.460
What?! Lady Julia, what have you done? Oh no!

00:11:16.880 --> 00:11:17.380
Huh?

00:11:17.380 --> 00:11:18.420
Wait, do you mean me?

00:11:18.420 --> 00:11:19.380
Could it be?!

00:11:20.540 --> 00:11:23.080
Six bogeys spotted incoming 
from the northwest.

00:11:23.280 --> 00:11:24.830
The Council Security Force and

00:11:24.830 --> 00:11:27.910
the Areshima Private Air
Security Squad are moving out to intercept.

00:11:27.910 --> 00:11:30.290
Wait. What should the Nazarin do?

00:11:30.290 --> 00:11:32.210
Patrol to the southeast.

00:11:32.210 --> 00:11:35.130
This is why I hate these government types.

00:11:35.130 --> 00:11:37.470
Always clinging to each other.

00:11:37.470 --> 00:11:39.330
There are only six targets.

00:11:39.330 --> 00:11:41.420
They probably just didn't want to crowd up.

00:11:41.830 --> 00:11:46.000
I bet they just want to score 
more hits for themselves.

00:11:46.000 --> 00:11:48.130
Adolfo, look to your two o'clock.

00:11:48.130 --> 00:11:50.710
What? Is there some babe 
or something out there?

00:11:51.420 --> 00:11:52.230
Huh?

00:11:59.210 --> 00:12:01.080
Areshima! The real fight is here!

00:12:07.880 --> 00:12:10.320
So we fell right for the bait, then?

00:12:10.320 --> 00:12:12.330
Mind if I share some more bad news?

00:12:12.710 --> 00:12:13.960
What might it be?

00:12:13.960 --> 00:12:18.500
This incoming group's got twenty 52s,
and probably two bombers.

00:12:18.500 --> 00:12:19.300
How wonderful!

00:12:19.670 --> 00:12:21.790
There are eight of us, including the Nazarin.

00:12:21.790 --> 00:12:26.300
So while those government boys make their way back,
you think you can hold 'em off?

00:12:26.300 --> 00:12:27.460
"Hold 'em off"?!

00:12:27.460 --> 00:12:28.170
Sorry!

00:12:28.170 --> 00:12:28.670
But...

00:12:28.670 --> 00:12:30.710
We're gonna take 'em all down!

00:12:42.460 --> 00:12:45.420
No matter how you go about this,
we're way outnumbered!

00:12:45.830 --> 00:12:46.960
Once the KOTOBUKI squad gets here...

00:12:46.960 --> 00:12:48.880
Then what? Look how many there are!

00:12:48.880 --> 00:12:50.790
We can't go down here!

00:12:51.290 --> 00:12:53.340
This is to rebuild the Nazarin Air Squad!

00:12:53.340 --> 00:12:56.250
Yeah, but we gotta survive first!

00:13:02.960 --> 00:13:03.880
Dammit!

00:13:04.420 --> 00:13:07.680
Oh my! I never thought
we'd be facing off against air pirates!

00:13:07.680 --> 00:13:09.130
Who are they even after?

00:13:09.130 --> 00:13:10.500
It's got to be you, Lady Julia!

00:13:10.500 --> 00:13:13.000
Someone as big and famous 
as you, you've gotta be it!

00:13:13.000 --> 00:13:14.040
I'm sure of it!

00:13:14.040 --> 00:13:16.130
What kind of awful excuse 
for flattery is that?

00:13:16.130 --> 00:13:17.710
Or do you really just have dirt for brains?

00:13:17.710 --> 00:13:20.000
Yup! Sure do!

00:13:21.040 --> 00:13:22.080
Look at that glare!

00:13:22.080 --> 00:13:23.580
That's scarier than any pirate out there!

00:13:23.580 --> 00:13:24.790
I almost peed myself in fright!

00:13:24.790 --> 00:13:25.670
How'd you hold up?

00:13:25.670 --> 00:13:26.960
It was a close call.

00:13:27.580 --> 00:13:29.170
How far off are the KOTOBUKI girls?

00:13:29.170 --> 00:13:31.080
They should make contact in seven minutes.

00:13:34.670 --> 00:13:35.620
I'm outta ammo!

00:13:35.620 --> 00:13:37.080
I'm dry, too!

00:13:37.080 --> 00:13:38.500
I'm taking off!

00:13:38.500 --> 00:13:40.210
No point in dying out here!

00:13:45.010 --> 00:13:46.380
This is not good.

00:13:50.000 --> 00:13:50.890
KOTOBUKI?!

00:13:50.890 --> 00:13:52.100
Is that her?!

00:13:57.210 --> 00:13:58.460
Are you all right?

00:13:58.460 --> 00:14:00.670
Looks like they tore 
quite a hole through you.

00:14:00.670 --> 00:14:01.500
Dammit!

00:14:01.500 --> 00:14:03.730
You girls just wanted us to take a beating,
so you could come in

00:14:03.730 --> 00:14:05.190
and sweep up after, didn't you?!

00:14:05.190 --> 00:14:06.830
Precisely!

00:14:06.830 --> 00:14:09.380
We can't carry you back to the airport, but do take
care!

00:14:09.380 --> 00:14:10.290
Gimme a break!

00:14:10.290 --> 00:14:11.130
Bye-bye!

00:14:11.130 --> 00:14:13.660
Those 52s are faster than your Hayabusas.

00:14:13.660 --> 00:14:15.160
And those bombers...

00:14:15.540 --> 00:14:17.120
My guess is Type 4 Heavy Bombers.

00:14:17.120 --> 00:14:19.540
They may be heavy bombers, but they're plenty
maneuverable.

00:14:19.540 --> 00:14:20.380
Stay sharp.

00:14:20.380 --> 00:14:21.170
Why thank you!

00:14:21.170 --> 00:14:21.790
Kylie!

00:14:21.790 --> 00:14:22.750
You're late.

00:14:22.750 --> 00:14:24.040
Stay in position!

00:14:24.040 --> 00:14:24.760
Sorry!

00:14:24.760 --> 00:14:29.090
What? I coulda swore that was Little Miss Pancake
who flew in a second ago.

00:14:29.090 --> 00:14:30.300
FUEL

00:14:29.420 --> 00:14:32.260
An ally who breaks formation 
is worse than any enemy.

00:14:33.130 --> 00:14:35.210
The KOTOBUKI girls know that well enough.

00:14:39.420 --> 00:14:40.540
What's their deal?

00:14:56.910 --> 00:14:57.750
Damn!

00:15:37.000 --> 00:15:38.420
What's your problem, Reona?

00:15:38.420 --> 00:15:40.780
You're doing exactly what 
you always tell me not to!

00:15:40.780 --> 00:15:43.000
She is gunning plenty of them down, though...

00:15:43.000 --> 00:15:43.670
Something's not right!

00:15:43.670 --> 00:15:48.170
I mean, Reona's always the one 
to fight all by-the-books!

00:15:48.170 --> 00:15:50.290
That's because she's our leader.

00:15:50.670 --> 00:15:52.330
This is how she really flies.

00:15:52.330 --> 00:15:55.130
Once an enemy is in her sights,
she thinks of nothing but taking them down.

00:15:55.500 --> 00:15:57.330
That's why she's called 
the "Tenacious Reona".

00:15:57.750 --> 00:15:59.040
It's been a long time 
since I've seen this side.

00:15:59.040 --> 00:16:00.540
Enemy coming in at six o'clock.

00:16:15.580 --> 00:16:17.210
The Type 4 Heavy Bomber, AKA Hiryu.

00:16:17.210 --> 00:16:19.330
Fitted with machine guns on its sides.

00:16:19.330 --> 00:16:20.660
Analysis? Danger!

00:16:24.210 --> 00:16:25.130
Kate!

00:16:31.210 --> 00:16:32.210
Kate, fall back!

00:16:35.010 --> 00:16:36.210
What are you doing?!

00:16:36.210 --> 00:16:39.890
Go ahead and get yourself hurt, Reona,
but don't let Kate take your fall!

00:16:40.250 --> 00:16:41.170
Kylie...

00:16:41.170 --> 00:16:43.210
If you're gonna go crazy, at least say so!

00:16:43.210 --> 00:16:44.350
We'll follow you!

00:16:47.960 --> 00:16:49.290
Sorry, Kylie...

00:16:49.290 --> 00:16:50.540
If you're gonna apologize 
do it to everyone else!

00:16:50.880 --> 00:16:52.670
Now then Reona, what's the plan?

00:16:53.130 --> 00:16:57.000
Isao, sir. Lady Julia. We 
must begin our evacuation.

00:16:57.000 --> 00:16:57.960
Not happening.

00:16:57.960 --> 00:16:59.200
And why, pray tell?

00:16:59.200 --> 00:17:00.580
I'm not evacuating.

00:17:01.040 --> 00:17:05.460
If I did, all I'd hear from all those assholes
once this is over is how I ran away.

00:17:05.790 --> 00:17:07.290
Well, no thanks.

00:17:07.290 --> 00:17:10.770
I'd have to agree. I'd hate 
to be called a coward.

00:17:10.770 --> 00:17:12.670
Then what shall we do?

00:17:12.670 --> 00:17:13.170
Voilà!

00:17:14.420 --> 00:17:16.040
What did I used to do, again?

00:17:16.040 --> 00:17:18.140
You drove a car.

00:17:18.140 --> 00:17:21.130
And you almost ran over 
two stupid little girls.

00:17:21.130 --> 00:17:22.290
That was just the other day.

00:17:22.290 --> 00:17:23.500
I'm talking like long, long ago.

00:17:23.500 --> 00:17:25.630
You used to be a magnificent flying ace.

00:17:25.630 --> 00:17:27.330
Which just might mean...?

00:17:27.330 --> 00:17:28.210
Might mean...?

00:17:28.540 --> 00:17:30.710
Maybe I can head out there and fight?

00:17:31.880 --> 00:17:33.250
Wh-what?

00:17:33.920 --> 00:17:35.350
So be it.

00:17:35.350 --> 00:17:36.670
Yay! That settles it!

00:17:36.670 --> 00:17:38.920
The Soaring Magician is back in action!

00:17:38.920 --> 00:17:40.000
Hold it right there!

00:17:40.000 --> 00:17:41.040
Don't you worry!

00:17:41.040 --> 00:17:43.580
It's like riding a bike, Lady Julia!

00:17:43.580 --> 00:17:44.960
Listen to me when I speak to you!

00:17:44.330 --> 00:17:46.000
What is a "bike", anyway?

00:17:46.000 --> 00:17:48.580
I will tell you all about them later on.

00:17:48.580 --> 00:17:49.250
Very well!

00:17:49.250 --> 00:17:50.380
Let's go, then.

00:17:52.710 --> 00:17:53.960
What? No way!

00:17:53.960 --> 00:17:56.080
How is a doof like that a pilot?

00:17:56.080 --> 00:17:58.150
But there's only one man with the name Isao

00:17:58.150 --> 00:18:01.180
who went on from being a pilot 
to run a massive corporation.

00:18:01.180 --> 00:18:03.710
Does he have no recollection of you, Reona?

00:18:04.080 --> 00:18:05.130
I don't know.

00:18:05.130 --> 00:18:08.420
Well then there's really no need
to repay him then, is there?

00:18:08.420 --> 00:18:09.210
Time to shirk!

00:18:09.210 --> 00:18:10.210
Not gonna happen!

00:18:10.210 --> 00:18:12.630
Reona hates being in debt, you see!

00:18:13.000 --> 00:18:15.290
All right. Find me an opening!

00:18:15.290 --> 00:18:17.170
I'll fly in there and aim for those Hiryu!

00:18:17.170 --> 00:18:18.100
Roger!

00:18:18.100 --> 00:18:19.630
Don't let them anywhere near Areshima!

00:18:35.790 --> 00:18:36.500
Now!

00:19:06.250 --> 00:19:07.290
You did it!

00:19:07.290 --> 00:19:09.120
Not yet! There's still another bomber!

00:19:18.170 --> 00:19:18.800
It's fast!

00:19:18.800 --> 00:19:20.000
I'll get it!

00:19:20.000 --> 00:19:21.010
It's all yours!

00:19:34.630 --> 00:19:36.880
Gosh darn it!

00:19:36.880 --> 00:19:38.380
Kylie! Chika! Don't push your luck!

00:19:38.380 --> 00:19:39.960
If we don't Areshima's done for!

00:19:44.380 --> 00:19:45.290
What's that?

00:19:45.290 --> 00:19:46.080
More enemies?

00:19:46.790 --> 00:19:47.410
No!

00:19:54.080 --> 00:19:56.000
Man, nothing beats flying!

00:19:56.000 --> 00:19:57.710
Indeed, sir.

00:20:00.630 --> 00:20:03.130
He was known as the Soaring Magician.

00:20:03.130 --> 00:20:06.330
An ace pilot from a squad in Ikesuka.

00:20:06.710 --> 00:20:10.030
Back during the Rinouchi 
Air War, he supposedly shot

00:20:10.030 --> 00:20:12.790
down twelve fighters in a single skirmish.

00:20:12.790 --> 00:20:13.750
Never heard of him!

00:20:13.750 --> 00:20:15.710
I haven't seen him for eight whole years.

00:20:16.880 --> 00:20:19.500
Reona, you were there at Rinouchi?

00:20:19.500 --> 00:20:22.380
I was. And I got so worked up
that I flew right into danger.

00:20:22.380 --> 00:20:23.750
And got myself shot down.

00:20:29.040 --> 00:20:30.420
The only reason I made it out alive...

00:20:30.880 --> 00:20:31.790
was thanks to him.

00:20:42.420 --> 00:20:43.460
What is he doing?

00:20:43.460 --> 00:20:44.430
He shoulda taken the shot!

00:20:49.170 --> 00:20:51.460
Firing from above is what 
anyone else would have done.

00:20:53.580 --> 00:20:54.500
I know!

00:20:55.040 --> 00:20:56.040
He's going at it from below!

00:21:02.700 --> 00:21:04.500
Excellent, sir.

00:21:05.250 --> 00:21:06.560
You truly are…

00:21:06.560 --> 00:21:08.330
The Soaring Magician!

00:21:09.380 --> 00:21:10.960
Shoot! I can't see!

00:21:10.960 --> 00:21:13.250
It's because you get so carried away.

00:21:13.250 --> 00:21:16.880
I swear I'll stop! Just help me!

00:22:04.470 --> 00:22:08.580
I wanted to try and soar through that sky

00:22:08.580 --> 00:22:12.390
So I wished upon the winds right before me

00:22:12.390 --> 00:22:16.330
Our aspirations build us scenery

00:22:16.330 --> 00:22:20.750
I wonder how that wind is now

00:22:25.000 --> 00:22:29.080
Why do we fight, I wonder

00:22:29.080 --> 00:22:33.130
What is our purpose here?

00:22:33.130 --> 00:22:41.380
I asked, but the skies do not answer

00:22:42.040 --> 00:22:49.040
We all have wings

00:22:49.040 --> 00:22:53.750
Far away at the end of all lament

00:22:53.750 --> 00:22:58.000
The stories we found

00:22:58.000 --> 00:23:05.730
No one can steal these skies away

00:23:05.730 --> 00:23:10.460
We will soar unafraid of anything

00:23:10.460 --> 00:23:17.630
Because happiness is right here

00:23:25.960 --> 00:23:27.460
Preview

00:23:33.470 --> 00:23:37.540
Next time on The Magnificent KOTOBUKI,
"No Place to Return"!

00:23:38.250 --> 00:23:41.000
No Place to Return
